<div class="bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100">
  <.marketing_nav current_user={@current_user} current={:docs} />

  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <.docs_layout
      current="integrations-entra"
      toc={[
        {"sso", "Single sign-on"},
        {"scim", "Directory sync"}
      ]}
    >
      <.docs_header current="integrations-entra">
        <:dek>
          Connect Microsoft Entra to emisar: an app registration signs people in with the oid claim,
          and a separate enterprise application provisions the directory.
        </:dek>
      </.docs_header>
      <.docs_prerequisites>
        <:item>An <strong class="text-zinc-300">Entra administrator</strong>.</:item>
        <:item>An emisar <strong class="text-zinc-300">owner or admin</strong>.</:item>
      </.docs_prerequisites>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        The sections below build two objects in order — sign-in first, then the directory.
      </p>

      <.docs_h2 id="sso">Single sign-on</.docs_h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        Connecting an identity provider is a paid feature. <.plan_note tier={:team} />
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-8 space-y-10">
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>emisar</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Start the connection.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Open
              <a
                href={~p"/app/sso/new"}
                class="font-medium text-brand-400 underline decoration-zinc-700 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-300"
              >Team → Single sign-on → Add provider</a>
              and choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Microsoft Entra ID</strong>. Leave the page open: the
              callback URL on it is what Entra asks for next, and Entra's values come back here
              at the end.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-emisar-add-provider.webp"
              title="emisar · Add provider"
              caption="Picking the provider here tailors the rest of the form to it."
              alt="emisar's Add provider form with the Provider type select outlined in green and set to Microsoft Entra ID."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Register the application.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              In the Microsoft Entra admin center go to <strong class="text-zinc-200">App registrations → New registration</strong>. Under
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Redirect URI</strong>
              choose the <strong class="text-zinc-200">Web</strong>
              platform and enter emisar's callback:
            </p>
            <.docs_code
              phx-no-format
              label="Redirect URI"
              copy_text="https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback"
            >https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback</.docs_code>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-app-registration.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra admin center · Register an application"
              caption="The platform must be set to Web — the URI beside it is ignored until it is, and the form refuses to register without it."
              alt="Entra's Register an application form with the name emisar, Supported account types set to Single tenant only, and the Redirect URI section outlined in green: its platform dropdown reads Web and the adjacent field holds https://emisar.dev/sign_in/sso/callback."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Create a client secret.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Certificates &amp; secrets → New client secret</strong>. Copy the
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Value</strong>
              column, not <strong class="text-zinc-200">Secret ID</strong>
              — the value is shown once and is unrecoverable afterwards.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-client-secret.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Certificates &amp; secrets"
              caption="Value is masked the moment you navigate away — the Secret ID beside it is not the secret, so copy the Value while it is still shown."
              alt="The app's Certificates and secrets blade, Client secrets tab, listing one secret named emisar SSO with an expiry date, a masked Value column, and a separate Secret ID column."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            4
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Copy the client and tenant IDs.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              The registration's <strong class="text-zinc-200">Overview</strong>
              blade carries both values emisar needs to identify your tenant:
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Application (client) ID</strong>
              is the client ID, and <strong class="text-zinc-200">Directory (tenant) ID</strong>
              is what goes into the issuer URL.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-app-overview.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · App registration overview"
              caption="Application (client) ID is emisar's Client ID. Directory (tenant) ID below it goes into the issuer."
              alt="The emisar app registration's Overview blade with Application (client) ID outlined in green, alongside Object ID, Directory (tenant) ID, client credentials showing one secret, and one web redirect URI."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            5
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>emisar</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Paste them into the connection.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Back on the connection you opened in step 1, the client ID is the
              <strong class="text-zinc-200">Application (client) ID</strong>
              and the secret is the one from step 3. Build the issuer from your tenant ID:
            </p>
            <.docs_code
              phx-no-format
              label="Issuer URL"
              copy_text="https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0"
            >https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0</.docs_code>
            <p class="mt-4">
              The trailing <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">/v2.0</code>
              is what selects Entra's v2.0 endpoint; without it you get v1.0 tokens. The
              identifier claim already reads
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">oid</code>
              — Entra hands every application a different <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">sub</code>, so
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">oid</code>
              is the only id that also matches what directory sync sends. Tick <strong class="text-zinc-200">Enabled</strong>, save, and sign in.
            </p>
            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-emisar-credentials.webp"
              title="emisar · Add provider"
              caption="The issuer carries your tenant ID and ends in /v2.0. The identifier claim is already oid."
              alt="emisar's OIDC connection fields with Issuer URL, Client ID and Client secret each outlined in green, the Issuer URL placeholder showing https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR-TENANT-ID/v2.0, and the Identifier claim reading oid — Microsoft Entra."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            1
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Create the enterprise application.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Provisioning does not live on the app registration you made for sign-in — it needs a
              separate object. Go to <strong class="text-zinc-200">Enterprise applications → New application → Create your own application</strong>, name it <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">emisar</code>, and choose <strong class="text-zinc-200">Integrate any other application you don't find in the gallery</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            2
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Point it at emisar.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              On the new application's <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning</strong>
              blade set <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning Mode</strong>
              to <strong class="text-zinc-200">Automatic</strong>, then fill in the two values emisar gave you —
              the SCIM base URL as <strong class="text-zinc-200">Tenant URL</strong>
              and the bearer as <strong class="text-zinc-200">Secret Token</strong>:
            </p>
            <.docs_code phx-no-format label="Tenant URL" copy_text="https://emisar.dev/scim/v2">https://emisar.dev/scim/v2</.docs_code>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-provisioning.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Enterprise application provisioning"
              caption="The Provisioning blade of the enterprise application — a different object from the app registration that handles sign-in. Connect your application is where the Tenant URL and Secret Token go."
              alt="The emisar SCIM enterprise application's Provisioning overview in the Entra portal, offering New configuration, Start provisioning and Pause provisioning in its command bar, with a Get started panel whose Create configuration step, outlined in green, holds a Connect your application button."
            />
            <p class="mt-4">
              Press <strong class="text-zinc-200">Test Connection</strong>. Entra probes the endpoint for a user that
              cannot exist, using a random GUID, and expects an empty result rather than an error —
              emisar answers that correctly, so a failure here means the URL or the token is wrong,
              not the schema. Save.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-provisioning-credentials.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · New provisioning configuration"
              caption="Leave the authentication method on Bearer. Secret token takes the ems- bearer, and Test connection sits directly beneath — Entra will not let you Create until it passes."
              alt="Entra's New provisioning configuration form for the emisar SCIM enterprise application, its Admin credentials block outlined in green: Select authentication method set to Bearer authentication, Tenant URL filled with https://emisar.dev/scim/v2, a filled but masked Secret token field, a Test connection button, and an enabled Create button below — Entra enables Create only once the test has passed."
            />
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            3
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Remap externalId to objectId.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Open <strong class="text-zinc-200">Manage → Attribute mapping</strong>
              and change the source attribute feeding
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">externalId</code>
              from <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">mailNickname</code>
              to <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">objectId</code>. On a tenant
              still using Entra's older provisioning screens, the same setting lives under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Mappings → Provision Microsoft Entra ID Users</strong>.
            </p>

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-attribute-mapping.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Attribute mapping"
              caption="The row to change, among about twenty: mailNickname is what Entra sends as externalId until you say otherwise."
              alt="The emisar SCIM application's Attribute mapping list on the Users tab, with columns for Source Attribute, Target Attribute, Mapping Type and Matching Precedence. The row mapping mailNickname to externalId is outlined in green, among rows for givenName, jobTitle, mail, manager and others."
            />

            <.docs_screenshot
              src="/images/docs/sso/entra-externalid-objectid.webp"
              title="Microsoft Entra · Edit Attribute Mapping"
              caption="Change the source, not the target — externalId stays put, because it is the field emisar keys on."
              alt="Entra's Edit Attribute Mapping pane with the Source attribute row outlined in green and set to objectId, alongside Mapping type Direct, Target attribute externalId, and Apply this mapping set to Always."
            />
            <p class="mt-4">
              Do not skip this. Entra's default is <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">mailNickname</code>, which is not guaranteed to exist, is not guaranteed to be
              unique, and can change — and it is not the value your sign-in connection identifies
              people by. With <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">oid</code>
              on the SSO side and
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">mailNickname</code>
              here, the same person arrives as two different identities: one provisioned by the
              directory, one created when they sign in.
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">objectId</code>
              is the same immutable id the
              <code class="rounded bg-zinc-900 px-1 py-0.5 text-xs">oid</code>
              claim carries, so the two halves converge.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="grid h-8 w-8 flex-none place-items-center rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-300">
            4
          </span>
          <div class="min-w-0 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
            <.docs_step_venue>Entra</.docs_step_venue>
            <p class="font-semibold text-zinc-100">Assign the people to sync.</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5">
              Under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Users and groups</strong>, assign whoever should exist in emisar, then
              turn <strong class="text-zinc-200">Provisioning Status</strong>
              on. Entra syncs on its own schedule — roughly every 40 minutes — so the first members
              appear under <strong class="text-zinc-200">Synced users</strong>
              on the emisar connection after that cycle, not instantly. Their Entra groups become
              mappable to roles below.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="mt-8 text-base leading-7 text-zinc-400">
        <strong class="text-zinc-200">Next:</strong>
        map directory groups to emisar roles so access follows your IdP — <.link
          navigate={~p"/docs/scim#role-mapping"}
          class="text-brand-300 underline decoration-brand-500/40 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-200"
        >role mapping</.link>.
      </p>
    </.docs_layout>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer />
</div>
